<title>FRANCE: Aerospatiale wins Arabsat contract.</title>
<headline>Aerospatiale wins Arabsat contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>SNI Aerospatiale said on Friday it has won a contract as prime contractor to build the Arabsat II-BSS1 generation of telecommunications satellites for the Arabsat operator.</p>
<p>The contract is for contruction of the satellite, which will be delivered in 24 months. The payload will be built by Alcatel Espace, a unit of Alcatel Alsthom. The satellite will use the Spacebus 3000 platform developed with Daimler-Benz Aerospace.</p>
<p>No financial details were available. The satellite will be used mainly for direct to home television broadcasting.</p>
</text>
